positive_text:
Consideriamo una griglia $2n \times 2n$, e un insieme $S$ di celle. Diciamo che $S$ è un labirinto se soddisfa le seguenti condizioni:
- ogni cella di $S$ è raggiungibile da ogni altra cella di $S$ seguendo un percorso che utilizza solo celle di $S$ adiacenti (in orizzontale o verticale);
- non è possibile tornare alla stessa cella di partenza seguendo un percorso all'interno di $S$ senza mai ripetere un lato.

a. Mostrare che se $S$ è un labirinto, allora $|S| \leq 3n^{2}$;

b. Costruire un esempio di labirinto con 12 celle quando $n=2$;

c. Definiamo il perimetro di $S$ come il numero di lati che sono adiacenti a una sola cella di $S$. Se $S$ è un labirinto con $k$ celle, determinare il valore del suo perimetro;

d. Dimostrare che non esiste un labirinto con 300 celle per $n=10$.

Given $n$ distinct individuals, each initially possessing a unique item. A sequence of pairwise exchanges is conducted such that in each exchange, two individuals swap the items they currently hold. Every pair of individuals must exchange items at least once during the process. If all individuals eventually return to holding their original item, determine the minimal number of exchanges required, for:
a) $n=5$;
b) $n=6$.

negatives.text:
In a group of $n$ people, each one had a different ball. They performed a sequence of swaps; in each swap, two people swapped the ball they had at that moment. Each pair of people performed at least one swap. In the end, each person had a different ball than the one he/she had at the start. Find the least possible number of swaps, if:
a) $n=5$;
b) $n=6$.

In a group of $n$ people, each one had a different ball. They performed a sequence of swaps; in each swap, two people swapped the ball they had at that moment. Each pair of people performed at least one swap. In the end, each person had the ball he/she had at the start. Find the least possible number of swaps, if:
a) $n=5$;
b) $n=7$.

In a group of $n$ people, each one had a different ball. They performed a sequence of swaps; in each swap, two people swapped the ball they had at that moment. Each pair of people performed at least one swap. In the end, each person had the ball he/she had at the start. Find the least possible number of swaps, if:
a) $n=5$;
b) $n=6$. The number of swaps must be even.

