Let $S$ be a finite non-empty set of prime numbers. Define $|S|$ as the number of elements in $S$, and let $n(S)$ denote the maximum number of consecutive positive integers such that each is divisible by at least one element of $S$.
(a) Prove that $|S| \le n(S)$, and equality holds precisely when the smallest element of $S$ is greater than $|S|$;
(b) Prove that $n(S) < (|S| + 1)(2^{|S|} - 1)$.

negatives.text:
