positive_text:
a. Let $A_{n} = \{a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n}, x\}$, for $n \geq 3$, and let $C_{n}$ be the 2-configuration consisting of $\{a_{i}, a_{i+1}\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq n-1$, $\{a_{1}, a_{n}\}$, and $\{a_{i}, x\}$ for $1 \leq i \leq n$. Let $T_{e}(n)$ be the number of subsets of $C_{n}$ that are consistent of order $e$. Find $T_{e}(101)$ for $e=1,2$, and $3$.

b. Let $A = \{P, Q, R, S, T, p, q, r, s, t\}$. Find the number of subsets of the 2-configuration
$$
\begin{gathered}
\{\{P, Q\},\{Q, R\},\{R, S\},\{S, T\},\{T, P\},\{p, r\},\{p, s\},\{q, s\},\{q, t\},\{r, t\}, \\
\{P, p\},\{Q, q\},\{R, r\},\{S, s\},\{T, t\}\}
\end{gathered}
$$
that are consistent of order 1.

c. Let $A = \{u_{1}, v_{1}, u_{2}, v_{2}, \ldots, u_{10}, v_{10}\}$, and consider the 2-configuration $C$ consisting of $\{u_{i}, v_{i}\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq 10$, $\{u_{i}, u_{i+1}\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq 9$, and $\{v_{i}, v_{i+1}\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq 9$. Find the number of subsets of $C$ that are consistent of order 1.

Let
$$
T(n, r)=\binom{n-1}{r-1}+\binom{n-1}{r}+\binom{n-1}{r+1}+\cdots+\binom{n-1}{n-1}
$$
for all $n, r>0$, with $T(n, r)=0$ if $r>n>0$. Show that the value at position $n$, $r$ steps to the left of the leading 1 in the top row of the table, is no greater than $T(n, r)$. (Hint: Begin by verifying that $T(n-1, r-1)+T(n-1, r)=T(n, r)$.)

\text{Problem:}\\
\begin{align*}
&c_{k}= \begin{cases}1 & \text{ if } k \text{ is divisible by } 3 \\ 0 & \text{ otherwise }\end{cases}\\
&\text{Let }\{x_{k}\}\text{ be a binary sequence such that}\\
