&\text{for all }k \in \{0,1,\dots,59\}\text{ (with }x_{0}=x_{60}\text{ and }x_{-1}=x_{59}\text{). Determine all values of }4 x_{0}+2 x_{1}+x_{2}.\end{align*}

Determine the number of sequences $(x_{1}, y_{1}), (x_{2}, y_{2}), \ldots, (x_{10}, y_{10})$ of pairs of integers such that:

- Each $x_{i}, y_{i} \in \{1, 2, \ldots, 10\}$;
- The sequence $x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{10}$ is non-decreasing;
- Whenever $x_{i} = x_{i+1}$, it holds that $y_{i} \leq y_{i+1}$.

negatives.text:
