Let $f(x) = x^{2} - a x + b$ for all real numbers $x$, where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers. Define a sequence $\{h_{n}\}$ for all nonnegative integers $n$ by $h_{0} = 0$ and $h_{n+1} = f(h_{n})$. Assume that $\{h_{n}\}$ satisfies the following three conditions:

(i) $h_{2i} < h_{2i+1}$ and $h_{2i+1} > h_{2i+2}$ for all $0 \leq i \leq 2011$;

(ii) there exists a positive integer $k$ such that $h_{i+1} > h_{i}$ for all $i > k$;

(iii) $\{h_{n}\}$ is unbounded.

If $B$ is the greatest number such that $B \leq |a|$ for any function $f$ satisfying these properties, find $B$.

negatives.text:
